      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When onion cells are damaged, the enzyme alliinase reacts with the sulfur-containing compound S-alkencysteine sulfinate to produce syn-propanethial-S-oxide. This volatile lachrymatory factor vapors travel from the cut surface to your eyes, where it reacts with water in your tears to form mildly acidic sulfurous aerosols that stimulate your nerve endings. This chemical cascade triggers the tear ducts to produce excessive tears as a protective response. You might also notice that chopping onions with a sharp knife or letting them sit allows that stinging sensation to dissipate faster.",
