      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The difficulty lies in the inherent volatility of the lachrymatory factor, which evaporates rapidly into the air regardless of the crop's size or type. Unlike water or salt, these specific sulfur compounds disperse quickly on their own, making containment through ventilation or knife-sharpening techniques less effective without immediate action. This rapid diffusion means the concentration of irritant at your face can spike suddenly, bypassing your ability to simply \"let it settle\" before it becomes too potent. As a result, management requires active physical barriers rather than passive waiting, which disrupts the natural flow of chopping and feels counterintuitively difficult for students.",
